+## Incremental cache
+
+Use `--cache` to persist per-file analysis results between runs:
+
+    $ vulture --cache mydir
+
+The cache is stored in `.vulture-cache/` by default. Set another location with
+`--cache-dir=PATH`. On later runs, Vulture only analyzes changed files and
+files which transitively import them. Unchanged results are loaded from the
+cache.
+Runtime, analysis-setting, and bundled-whitelist changes automatically
+invalidate the affected cache entries.
+
+Use `--cache-clear` to remove everything in the cache directory before the
+scan. It also enables caching for that run:
+
+    $ vulture --cache-clear --cache-dir=/tmp/vulture-cache mydir
+
